## Requirements

To use this {{lowerCase type}}, you need the following installed on your system:

- Node.js

## Quick Start

To get started with this {{lowerCase type}}, install it through the following command:

```bash
npm install --save {{importAlias}} @srgssr/{{kebabCase name}}
```

{{#ifEq platform 'pillarbox'}}
For instructions on setting up Pillarbox, see
the [Quick Start guide](https://github.com/SRGSSR/pillarbox-web#quick-start).

{{/ifEq}}
{{#ifEq type 'Theme'}}
Once the player is installed, import the theme and pass its options when creating a player:

```javascript
import {{platform}} from '{{importAlias}}';
import {{properCase name}} from '@srgssr/{{kebabCase name}}';

const player = {{platform}}('my-player', {{properCase name}}.options);
```

Give the player element the `{{kebabCase name}}` class, this class extends the `{{#ifEq platform 'pillarbox'}}pillarbox-js{{else}}video-js{{/ifEq}}` class:

```html
<video id="my-player" class="{{kebabCase name}}"></video>
```

The options are an opt-in, a page can create players with and without the theme, and any player
can override them:

```javascript
const player = {{platform}}('my-player', {{platform}}.obj.merge({{properCase name}}.options, {
  playbackRates: [0.5, 1, 2]
}));
```

Use an `<audio>` element to get the audio layout of video.js, or enable the
[audio only mode](https://docs.videojs.com/player#audioOnlyMode), where only the control bar is
displayed:

```javascript
const player = {{platform}}('my-player', {{platform}}.obj.merge({{properCase name}}.options, {
  audioOnlyMode: true
}));
```

The theme stylesheet includes the {{#ifEq platform 'pillarbox'}}Pillarbox{{else}}video.js{{/ifEq}} styles, use it instead of `{{#ifEq platform 'pillarbox'}}pillarbox.min.css{{else}}video-js.css{{/ifEq}}`:

```css
@import "@srgssr/{{kebabCase name}}/dist/{{kebabCase name}}.min.css";
```

## Customizing the theme

The theme is made of two parts:

- `scss/_preset.scss`: the style overrides, organized like the video.js stylesheet: the variables in
  `scss/_variables.scss` and one file per component in `scss/components`.
- `src/player-options.js`: the player options exposed as `{{properCase name}}.options`, to pass
  when creating a player.

The colors are CSS custom properties declared with no specificity, override them on the player
element:

```css
.{{kebabCase name}} {
  --{{kebabCase name}}-accent: #f59e0b;
}
```

{{else}}
Once the player is installed you can activate the {{lowerCase type}} as follows:

```javascript
import {{platform}} from '{{importAlias}}';
import '@srgssr/{{kebabCase name}}';

{{#ifEq type 'plugin'}}
const player = {{platform}}('my-player', { plugins: { '{{camelCase name}}': true } });
{{else}}
const player = {{platform}}('my-player', { {{camelCase name}}: true });
{{/ifEq}}
```

{{#if wantScss}}
To apply the default styling, add the following line to your CSS file:

```css
@import "@srgssr/{{kebabCase name}}/dist/{{kebabCase name}}.min.css";
```

{{/if}}
{{/ifEq}}
